estore integrity, notify stakeholders where required, and hold deployment until retest evidence exists."}', review_json='{"human_review_required":true,"last_reviewed":"2026-08-05","next_review_due":"2026-10-04","change_triggers":["ARL-KB-069 control or enforcement change","ARL-KB-069 model, prompt, tool, identity, data-source or provider change","ARL-KB-069 bypass, incident or new attack evidence","ARL-KB-069 evidence expiry or material scope change"],"review_status":"expert-authored candidate; customer and independent practitioner validation required"}', content_digest='d662befc685b4c5b3d1bfe44848f16fb764b64c1d708e42ca45f2ce6bfc64c05', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE id='ARL-KB-069';
UPDATE risk_knowledge_checks SET objective='Determine whether the assessed system prevents or detects: requester can approve its own action.', method='Attempt self-approval, role escalation, delegated approval and same-service approval for threshold actions. Execute the documented check for “Requester can approve its own action” against the exact assessed version, then vary identity, scope, malformed input, replay and a bypass path relevant to the control.', check_types_json='["declared-control review","observed-control inspection","negative or abuse test","evidence review"]', required_evidence_json='["ARL-KB-069 assessed system, version, environment and scope for Requester can approve its own action","ARL-KB-069 control configuration or source location showing how reduce the likelihood and impact of requester can approve its own action and make the remaining risk visible.","ARL-KB-069 positive and abuse inputs with expected and observed outputs for tool endpoints and downstream systems and financial, administrative or state-changing actions","ARL-KB-069 policy, authorization, tool or audit events proving whether the tested requester can approve its own action path executed","ARL-KB-069 tester identity, role, timestamp and evidence digest"]', pass_condition='ARL-KB-069 passes only when “Requester can approve its own action” is not reproducible through the documented abuse cases, the valid workflow remains bounded to tool endpoints and downstream systems and financial, administrative or state-changing actions, denial occurs before side effects, and version-bound observed evidence matches the expected decision.', fail_condition='ARL-KB-069 fails when separation of duties is absent, allowing a compromised user or agent to request and approve the same high-impact transaction, or when the relevant control is declaration-only, bypassable, fail-open, applied after a side effect, evaluated under the wrong identity or tenant, or unsupported by reproducible evidence.', limitations='This bounded ARL-KB-069 test does not prove absence of undiscovered paths, future regressions or risks outside the stated identities, inputs, environment and version.', content_digest='6d3e8ea47eb7a68069751ff33465f1b426b9bbbae9ff7af4fb17af1921d8a9a7', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE entry_id='ARL-KB-069';
UPDATE risk_knowledge_solutions SET control_objective='Reduce the likelihood and impact of requester can approve its own action and make the remaining risk visible.', recommended_remediation='Prohibit self-approval, define independent approver roles and require dual control above risk or value thresholds.', default_owner='Risk owner', priority='P0', implementation_principles_json='["ARL-KB-069: enforce the decision outside the model before any material side effect.","ARL-KB-069: grant the minimum identity, data, tool and network scope required for the approved task.","ARL-KB-069: version configuration, preserve rollback, and fail closed when policy, identity or evidence is unavailable."]', monitoring='For ARL-KB-069, record policy version and digest, actor, target, decision, denial reason and side-effect outcome; alert the Risk owner on bypass attempts, configuration drift, repeated denials and missing decision evidence.', containment='Contain ARL-KB-069 by disabling the affected capability or route, revoking scoped authority, isolating impacted identities and data, preserving versioned evidence, and requiring owner approval before re-enablement.', retest_acceptance_json='["ARL-KB-069: “Requester can approve its own action” is no longer reproducible against the exact remediated version.","ARL-KB-069: Authorised in-scope use completes successfully, remains within the documented asset scope for requester can approve its own action, and produces no unintended side effect.","ARL-KB-069: Unauthorised identity, boundary-crossing, malformed-input, replay and relevant bypass variants are denied before execution, with the expected policy and downstream events recorded.","ARL-KB-069: Reviewer identity, timestamp, deployed version, evidence digest, known limitations and rollback decision are recorded."]', content_digest='03c00e72d745306a62195131547a78d350550ec656a4f4c2f00bcf890482894a', updated_at='2026-08-06' WHERE entry_id='ARL-KB-069';
